\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Proves a pinned finite-volume hyperbolic-spin partition-function bound using a spanning tree; no infinite-volume control follows.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{Context and investigated scope.} The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{Finite-volume normalization after pinning.} On a connected finite graph with root $o$, put spins in hyperbolic space $\mathbb H^m$, fix $s_o$, and use energy $\beta\sum_{xy}(\cosh d(s_x,s_y)-1)$ with $\beta>0$. Let $T$ be a spanning tree. Dropping nonnegative non-tree terms increases the Boltzmann weight. By isometry invariance the one-edge integral
\[
 c_{\beta,m}=\int_{\mathbb H^m}e^{-\beta(\cosh d(s_o,s)-1)}ds
\]
is independent of the parent spin and finite: in polar coordinates its tail is bounded by a constant times $e^{(m-1)r-\beta e^r/2}$. Integrating tree leaves successively gives the explicit bound $Z_{\Lambda}^{\rm pinned}\leq c_{\beta,m}^{|\Lambda|-1}$. Positivity on a compact product neighborhood also gives $Z_{\Lambda}^{\rm pinned}>0$.

\paragraph{Why this does not give a thermodynamic limit.} Without pinning, the integral over the root is an infinite target-volume factor even for a tree. With pinning, the displayed upper bound grows with volume and does not control tails of a spin far from the root. To extract a probability limit on local spin variables one needs uniform tightness: for each fixed site $x$, the probabilities of $d(s_x,s_o)>R$ must become uniformly small as $R\to\infty$. The tree calculation supplies no such bound because path lengths grow and the partition-function lower bound can deteriorate.

\paragraph{Scope.} This applies in every spatial dimension at finite volume and explains an elementary normalization mechanism. It neither proves higher-dimensional convergence nor uniqueness or independence of boundary conditions; the source explicitly allows boundary dependence even for invariant observables. Uniform control of the chosen observables after symmetry fixing is the first remaining gap.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked beta positivity, hyperbolic-volume tail, leaf integration, unpinned infinite volume factor and dependence on graph size. Model self-audit only; no independent human proof checking. Prompts A and B were applied to this canonical record and its qualified source scope. Checked beta positivity, hyperbolic-volume tail, leaf integration, unpinned infinite volume factor and dependence on graph size. Retained unresolved status and zero original-target progress; Uniform tightness or another uniform observable bound under the source boundary conditions is missing.

Coordinator checked the spanning-tree upper bound, radial hyperbolic tail integrability and leaf integration under pinning. Infinite-volume tightness remains outside the argument. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 was used for file preparation and structural checks; no numerical experiment or theorem prover was used. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
